division by `n` in `cap no_panic` module may be by zero — no refinement proves `n ≠ 0`. [division_by_zero]

`n` is not a function parameter, so no refinement annotation reaches it. Guard the division instead, which the checker reads as proof: `if n == 0 do <fallback> else ... / n end`. Or use `Math.checked_div` or `Math.checked_mod`, which return `Option(Int)` instead of panicking.

